# Hedda Ironvow's camp talks (story/camp_talk.gd). Quest: Cold Prayers (narrative/companions/prayers.dialogue).

~ talk_cold
if name:hedda_ironvow and flag.burgomaster_buried and flag.eva_truth_teller != "hedda_ironvow" and not (quest.cold_prayers >= cold)
-> cold
endif
-> END

~ cold
Narrator: Hedda prays at the end of every day, aloud, the way her chapel taught her. Tonight she stops halfway through and sits back on her heels, and stays there.
interject name:hedda_ironvow: Mm. Come and sit, if you're going to stare. It's warmer by the fire. That's more than I can say for my god.
* What's wrong? -> cold_what
* (Sit with her.) -> cold_what

~ cold_what
interject name:hedda_ironvow: Since we came through the mist I haven't felt Him. Not once. The prayers still answer. The wounds still close. But it's like warming your hands at a painting of a fire.
interject name:hedda_ironvow: Back home the first light of every day struck our altar, and you could feel it on your face like a hand. Here it's grey, and the spells come cold, and I do them anyway.
interject name:hedda_ironvow: I haven't told anyone. A healer who doubts is a healer nobody wants near the bed.
* Your spells kept us alive. Cold or not. -> cold_alive
* Maybe He's further away here. That's not the same as gone. -> cold_far
* What would make it warm again? -> cold_what_warm

~ cold_alive
interject name:hedda_ironvow: Mm. They did. That's the thing that frightens me. If it works without Him, what was He ever for?
interject name:hedda_ironvow: ...No. Don't answer that. That's a question for a long winter, and we're busy.
-> cold_end

~ cold_far
interject name:hedda_ironvow: Further away. Yes. Stone remembers, and sun warms stone from a long way off, if it gets the chance. Thank you. That is a better sermon than I would have managed tonight.
-> cold_end

~ cold_what_warm
interject name:hedda_ironvow: The dream, I think. The silver raven and its little sun. I didn't come here because I was told to. I came because I wanted to see something warm in a cold place. I still want to.
-> cold_end

~ cold_end
if not (quest.cold_prayers >= cold)
quest cold_prayers cold
endif
interject name:ilse_varga: For what it's worth, cold prayers stitched my arm twice. I'll take cold.
interject name:silvain_aster: Silvain Aster, also alive on cold prayers. Present and grateful. Please go back to sleep, Hedda.
-> END

~ talk_warmth
if name:hedda_ironvow and quest.find_the_holy_symbol == found
-> warmth
endif
-> END

~ warmth
Narrator: Hedda doesn't pray tonight. She sits with the Holy Symbol of Ravenkind in both hands, the silver raven and its sunburst, and doesn't say anything for a long time.
interject name:hedda_ironvow: It's warm.
interject name:hedda_ironvow: Not the sun. Not yet. A coal somebody kept alive in a cupped hand for three hundred years, waiting for someone to blow on it.
if flag.hedda_spark_felt
interject name:hedda_ironvow: The same warmth I felt in St. Andral's, for that one breath. I wasn't imagining it. Mm. I'm glad. I was afraid I had.
endif
if flag.eva_question == "dawn"
interject name:hedda_ironvow: Madam Eva said carry it into his house and I'd see the difference. Mm. I believe her now. I'd like to see his face.
endif
interject name:hedda_ironvow: Thank you. All of you. You walked me to it, and I was too proud to say I couldn't find it on my own.
interject name:tamsin_tealeaf: Can I hold it? Just for a second. I won't steal it. I'd like to know what holy feels like before I'm too old to try being it.
interject name:hedda_ironvow: Mm. Hold it, little thief. It doesn't mind who it warms. That's rather the point.
if not (quest.cold_prayers >= warmth)
quest cold_prayers warmth
endif
-> END
